I removed the two Gemini ids Google never listed, moved the google default to gemini-3.8-flash, and committed it as f7e9620d ("Part of #1021"). Build, the full test suite, clippy with -D warnings and the fmt check all pass.

Re-measured first. I re-ran the curl/grep against Google's model page myself. It lists 41 gemini-* strings, and gemini-3.0-pro and gemini-3.0-flash appear 0 times, the same as when #1021 was filed. The output is in the commit body.

Removed:
• Both ids are gone from the google known list in src/providers.rs.
• In the /model <Tab> completion list in src/commands.rs, I replaced them with gemini-4-argon and gemini-3.8-flash, so the new default shows up there.
• The task mentioned "1,048,576 pins" in model_context_window. There weren't any: the function matches anything containing gemini-3. Only a test asserted those two ids, and it now uses ids from Google's page (gemini-3.1-pro-preview, gemini-3-flash-preview).

Other places that used `gemini-3.0`. None of these is shown to users:
• In src/format/cost.rs, the pricing tests and comments now use page ids that land on the same estimated-price rule.
• In the price audit tests, an alias table mapped Google's spelling to the gemini-3.0 one, with a comment saying yoyo ships gemini-3.0-*. That's no longer true, so I emptied the table and changed its test to check that Google's own spelling is priced directly.

New default: `gemini-3.8-flash`. I added a test written over whatever the google default is, mirroring the existing anthropic and openai ones. It checks three things:
• (a) yoagent has a preset for the id;
• (b) the preset is priced;
• (c) its default request (65,536 output tokens) fits within the declared ceiling (also 65,536).

The same test confirms the old default gemini-2.5-flash fails (a): yoagent only has google presets for gemini-4-argon and gemini-3.8-flash, so the old default was running on guessed limits. I picked Flash over Argon because it's the same tier as the old default.

Docs. Three pages (models.md, installation.md, guides/fork.md) said the google default was gemini-2.0-flash, which was already wrong before this change. All three now say gemini-3.8-flash.

Still open. I commented on #1021 with what changed, the new default, the sha and what's left. The main gap: yoyo knows 6 Gemini ids against the page's 41, so ids like gemini-3.1-pro-preview or gemini-3.7-flash still get an estimated window and price rather than a real one.
